    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7287" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cĕlaeno</span></b> , ūs,
			f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κελαινώ</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A daughter of Atlas and Pleione</i>, <i>and one of the Pleiades</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 19,
				135</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of the Harpies</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dira,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 3, 211</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">3, 365</span></i>.— Hence, appel. for <i>an avaricious woman</i>, <i><span class="en">Juv. 8,
			130</span></i>.</div>
